  "layout_note": "Single-column display title page set inside an ornamental woodcut interlace border (border is art only — no motto text is set within the border itself). Top: large display capitals; then a roman-prose descriptive block with small-caps emphasis words (ARGVMENTS, ANNOTATIONS, CORRVPTIONS); then two centered scripture citations — Pſal. 118 and S. Aug. — each followed by small, faded ITALIC Latin and a roman English 'That is' translation; imprint block at foot. WHOLE PAGE uses VV for W (no real 'w' sort anywhere: NEVV, vvith, Vvith, lavv, vvhich); u/v and i/j are period-swapped (IESVS, FAITHFVLLY, vnder, diuers). A modern red digital watermark (a URL) and a modern emblem at the foot are NOT part of the 1582 print and are excluded.",
  "body": [
    {"line_index": 0, "role": "title_display", "text": "THE"},
    {"line_index": 1, "role": "title_display", "text": "NEVV TESTAMENT"},
    {"line_index": 2, "role": "title_display", "text": "OF IESVS CHRIST, TRANS-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 3, "role": "title_display", "text": "LATED FAITHFVLLY INTO ENGLISH,"},
    {"line_index": 4, "role": "prose", "text": "out of the authentical Latin , according to the beſt cor-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 5, "role": "prose", "text": "rected copies of the ſame , diligently conferred vvith"},
    {"line_index": 6, "role": "prose", "text": "the Greeke and other editions in diuers languages: Vvith"},
    {"line_index": 7, "role": "prose", "text": "ARGVMENTS of bookes and chapters, ANNOTA-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 8, "role": "prose", "text": "TIONS, and other neceſſarie helpes, for the better vnder-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 9, "role": "prose", "text": "ſtanding of the text, and ſpecially for the diſcouerie of the"},
    {"line_index": 10, "role": "prose", "text": "CORRVPTIONS of diuers late tranſlations, and for"},
    {"line_index": 11, "role": "prose", "text": "cleering the CONTROVERSIES in religion, of theſe daies:"},
    {"line_index": 12, "role": "heading", "text": "IN THE ENGLISH COLLEGE OF RHEMES."},
    {"line_index": 13, "role": "heading", "text": "Pſal. 118."},
    {"line_index": 14, "role": "latin", "text": "Da mihi intellectum , & ſcrutabor legem tuam, & cuſtodiam"},
    {"line_index": 15, "role": "latin", "text": "illam in toto corde meo."},
    {"line_index": 16, "role": "heading", "text": "That is,"},
    {"line_index": 17, "role": "prose", "text": "Giue me vnderſtanding, and I vvil ſearche thy lavv, and"},
    {"line_index": 18, "role": "prose", "text": "vvil keepe it vvith my vvhole hart."},
    {"line_index": 19, "role": "heading", "text": "S. Aug. tract. ⟨2?⟩. in Epiſt. Ioan.", "has_uncertain": true},
    {"line_index": 20, "role": "latin", "text": "Omnia quæ leguntur in Scripturis ſanctis, ad inſtructionem & ſalutem noſtram intente oportet"},
    {"line_index": 21, "role": "latin", "text": "audire: maxime tamen memoriæ commendanda ſunt, quæ aduerſus Hæreticos valent plu-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 22, "role": "latin", "text": "rimum, quorum inſidiæ infirmiores quoſque negligentiores, circumuenire non ceſſant."},
    {"line_index": 23, "role": "heading", "text": "That is,"},
    {"line_index": 24, "role": "prose", "text": "Al things that are readde in holy Scriptures, vve muſt heare vvith great attention, to our"},
    {"line_index": 25, "role": "prose", "text": "inſtruction and ſaluation: but thoſe things ſpecially muſt be commended to me-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 26, "role": "prose", "text": "morie, vvhich make moſt againſt Heretikes: vvhoſe deceites ceaſe not to cir-", "line_end_hyphen": true},
    {"line_index": 27, "role": "prose", "text": "cumuent and beguile al the vveaker ſort and the more negligent perſons."},
    {"line_index": 28, "role": "imprint", "text": "PRINTED AT RHEMES,"},
    {"line_index": 29, "role": "imprint", "text": "by Iohn Fogny."},
    {"line_index": 30, "role": "imprint", "text": "1582."},
    {"line_index": 31, "role": "imprint", "text": "CVM PRIVILEGIO."}
  ],
